{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Dufy3ZF2XP4T6KudhCc7D6","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→use crate::types::TankState;\n     2→\n     3→const FEED_P_TO_N_MASS_RATIO: f64 = 0.10;\n     4→\n     5→/// Result of one hourly nitrogen cycle step, carrying coupling values\n     6→/// that downstream systems (DO, chemistry) need.\n     7→#[derive(Debug, Clone, Copy, Default)]\n     8→pub struct NitrogenCycleOutput {\n     9→    /// Total mg N oxidized to nitrate this tick (AOB + NOB + comammox pathway).\n    10→    pub total_mg_n_nitrified: f64,\n    11→}\n    12→\n    13→/// Monod-style environmental factors shared across guilds.\n    14→struct EnvFactors {\n    15→    f_temp: f64,\n    16→    f_ph: f64,\n    17→    maturity_factor: f64,\n    18→    /// Dirty-filter penalty: 1.0 = clean, lower = clogged/dirty.\n    19→    dirty_filter_factor: f64,\n    20→}\n    21→\n    22→fn safe_rate(v: f64) -> f64 {\n    23→    if v.is_finite() {\n    24→        v.max(0.0)\n    25→    } else {\n    26→        0.0\n    27→    }\n    28→}\n    29→\n    30→/// Runs the full nitrogen-cycle phase for one hourly tick.\n    31→///\n    32→/// Order: feed leaching -> detritus breakdown/mineralization -> nitrification + guild growth/decay.\n    33→///\n    34→/// Returns coupling values for downstream DO and alkalinity systems.\n    35→pub fn step_nitrogen_cycle(state: &mut TankState) -> NitrogenCycleOutput {\n    36→    let volume_l = state.geometry.water_volume_l();\n    37→    if volume_l <= f64::EPSILON {\n    38→        return NitrogenCycleOutput::default();\n    39→    }\n    40→\n    41→    let pp = &state.process_params;\n    42→\n    43→    // ---- 1. Feed leaching: particulate -> fine detritus ----\n    44→    let leach_rate = safe_rate(pp.feed_leach_rate_per_hour);\n    45→    let leached = (state.detritus.particulate_organics_g_total * leach_rate)\n    46→        .min(state.detritus.particulate_organics_g_total);\n    47→    state.detritus.particulate_organics_g_total -= leached;\n    48→    state.detritus.fine_detritus_g_total += leached;\n    49→\n    50→    // ---- 2. Fine detritus dissolution: fine detritus -> dissolved organic pools ----\n    51→    let diss_rate = safe_rate(pp.fine_detritus_dissolution_rate_per_hour);\n    52→    let dissolved = (state.detritus.fine_detritus_g_total * diss_rate)\n    53→        .min(state.detritus.fine_detritus_g_total);\n    54→    state.detritus.fine_detritus_g_total -= dissolved;\n    55→    // dissolved mass (g) -> mg for dissolved pools: 1 g = 1000 mg\n    56→    // Split into DOC and DON using N:C ratio\n    57→    let n_to_c = safe_rate(pp.feed_n_to_c_ratio);\n    58→    let doc_mg = dissolved * 1000.0 / (1.0 + n_to_c); // carbon fraction\n    59→    let don_mg = doc_mg * n_to_c; // nitrogen fraction\n    60→    let phosphate_mg = don_mg * FEED_P_TO_N_MASS_RATIO;\n    61→    state.water.dissolved_organic_carbon_mg_c_total += doc_mg;\n    62→    state.water.dissolved_organic_nitrogen_mg_n_total += don_mg;\n    63→    // Feed introduces dissolved phosphorus alongside organic C/N, supporting algae pressure.\n    64→    state.water.phosphate_mg_p_total += phosphate_mg;\n    65→    // Track flow through dissolved_feed_residue (bookkeeping, decremented by mineralization)\n    66→    state.detritus.dissolved_feed_residue_g_total += dissolved;\n    67→\n    68→    // ---- 3. Decomposer mineralization: DOC/DON -> TAN ----\n    69→    let decomposer_biomass = state.microbe.decomposer_biomass_g;\n    70→    let doc_total = state.water.dissolved_organic_carbon_mg_c_total;\n    71→    let don_total = state.water.dissolved_organic_nitrogen_mg_n_total;\n    72→    let do_total = state.water.dissolved_oxygen_mg_total;\n    73→\n    74→    // Environmental factors for decomposers\n    75→    let temp = state.water.temperature_c;\n    76→    let f_temp_decomp = temperature_factor(temp);\n    77→    let f_do_decomp = do_total / (do_total + 2.0); // half-sat ~2 mg total\n    78→\n    79→    // Microfauna modestly improve mineralization efficiency\n    80→    let microfauna_boost =\n    81→        1.0 + pp.microfauna_mineralization_boost * state.microfauna.population_index;\n    82→    let decomp_vmax = safe_rate(pp.decomposer_vmax_per_hour) * microfauna_boost;\n    83→    let k_doc = pp.decomposer_k_doc_mg.max(0.01);\n    84→    let monod_doc = doc_total / (doc_total + k_doc);\n    85→\n    86→    let potential_doc_consumed_mg = decomp_vmax * decomposer_biomass * 1000.0 // g->mg conversion for biomass effect\n    87→        * f_temp_decomp * f_do_decomp * monod_doc;\n    88→    let potential_doc_consumed_mg = safe_rate(potential_doc_consumed_mg);\n    89→\n    90→    // Clamp: cannot consume more DOC than exists\n    91→    let doc_consumed_mg = potential_doc_consumed_mg.min(doc_total);\n    92→    // Proportional DON consumed\n    93→    let don_consumed_mg = if doc_total > f64::EPSILON {\n    94→        doc_consumed_mg * (don_total / doc_total)\n    95→    } else {\n    96→        0.0\n    97→    };\n    98→    let don_consumed_mg = don_consumed_mg.min(don_total);\n    99→\n   100→    state.water.dissolved_organic_carbon_mg_c_total -= doc_consumed_mg;\n   101→    state.water.dissolved_organic_nitrogen_mg_n_total -= don_consumed_mg;\n   102→    // Mineralized DON becomes TAN\n   103→    state.water.ammonia_total_mg_n_total += don_consumed_mg;\n   104→    // Track residue pool depletion\n   105→    let residue_consumed_g = doc_consumed_mg / 1000.0 * (1.0 + n_to_c);\n   106→    state.detritus.dissolved_feed_residue_g_total =\n   107→        (state.detritus.dissolved_feed_residue_g_total - residue_consumed_g).max(0.0);\n   108→\n   109→    // Decomposer growth/decay\n   110→    let decomp_growth = safe_rate(pp.decomposer_growth_yield) * doc_consumed_mg / 1000.0; // mg->g\n   111→    let decomp_decay = safe_rate(pp.decomposer_decay_rate_per_hour) * decomposer_biomass;\n   112→    state.microbe.decomposer_biomass_g =\n   113→        (state.microbe.decomposer_biomass_g + decomp_growth - decomp_decay).max(0.0);\n   114→\n   115→    // ---- 4. Nitrification: TAN -> nitrite -> nitrate (+ comammox TAN -> nitrate) ----\n   116→    //\n   117→    // Shared DO and alkalinity budgets enforce that combined nitrification\n   118→    // can never consume more O2 or alkalinity than available this tick.\n   119→    let env = compute_env_factors(state);\n   120→    let combined_env = env.maturity_factor * env.dirty_filter_factor;\n   121→\n   122→    let mut do_budget = state.water.dissolved_oxygen_mg_total;\n   123→    let alk_per_mg_n = safe_rate(pp.alkalinity_meq_per_mg_n_nitrified);\n   124→    let mut alk_budget = state.water.alkalinity_meq_total;\n   125→\n   126→    // Stoichiometric O2 costs per mg N for each guild step\n   127→    let o2_for_aob = 3.43_f64; // TAN -> nitrite\n   128→    let o2_for_comammox = pp.o2_per_mg_n_nitrified; // TAN -> nitrate (4.57)\n   129→    let o2_for_nob = 1.14_f64; // nitrite -> nitrate\n   130→\n   131→    // 4a. AOB: TAN -> nitrite\n   132→    let aob_env_factor =\n   133→        combined_env * env.f_temp * env.f_ph * (do_budget / (do_budget + pp.aob_k_do_mg.max(0.01)));\n   134→    let aob_potential = monod_rate(\n   135→        safe_rate(pp.aob_vmax_mg_n_per_g_per_hour),\n   136→        state.microbe.ammonia_oxidizer_biomass_g,\n   137→        aob_env_factor,\n   138→        state.water.ammonia_total_mg_n_total,\n   139→        pp.aob_k_tan_mg.max(0.01),\n   140→    );\n   141→    let aob_rate = safe_rate(aob_potential)\n   142→        .min(state.water.ammonia_total_mg_n_total)\n   143→        .min(if o2_for_aob > 0.0 {\n   144→            do_budget / o2_for_aob\n   145→        } else {\n   146→            f64::MAX\n   147→        })\n   148→        .min(if alk_per_mg_n > 0.0 {\n   149→            alk_budget / alk_per_mg_n\n   150→        } else {\n   151→            f64::MAX\n   152→        });\n   153→\n   154→    // Debit shared budgets for AOB\n   155→    let aob_o2_cost = aob_rate * o2_for_aob;\n   156→    let aob_alk_cost = aob_rate * alk_per_mg_n;\n   157→    do_budget = (do_budget - aob_o2_cost).max(0.0);\n   158→    alk_budget = (alk_budget - aob_alk_cost).max(0.0);\n   159→\n   160→    // 4b. Comammox: TAN -> nitrate directly (lower vmax)\n   161→    let comammox_vmax = safe_rate(pp.aob_vmax_mg_n_per_g_per_hour * pp.comammox_vmax_fraction);\n   162→    let tan_after_aob = (state.water.ammonia_total_mg_n_total - aob_rate).max(0.0);\n   163→    let comammox_env_factor = combined_env\n   164→        * env.f_temp\n   165→        * env.f_ph\n   166→        * (do_budget / (do_budget + pp.comammox_k_do_mg.max(0.01)));\n   167→    let comammox_potential = monod_rate(\n   168→        comammox_vmax,\n   169→        state.microbe.comammox_biomass_g,\n   170→        comammox_env_factor,\n   171→        tan_after_aob,\n   172→        pp.comammox_k_tan_mg.max(0.01),\n   173→    );\n   174→    let comammox_rate = safe_rate(comammox_potential)\n   175→        .min(tan_after_aob)\n   176→        .min(if o2_for_comammox > 0.0 {\n   177→            do_budget / o2_for_comammox\n   178→        } else {\n   179→            f64::MAX\n   180→        })\n   181→        .min(if alk_per_mg_n > 0.0 {\n   182→            alk_budget / alk_per_mg_n\n   183→        } else {\n   184→            f64::MAX\n   185→        });\n   186→\n   187→    // Debit shared budgets for comammox\n   188→    let comammox_o2_cost = comammox_rate * o2_for_comammox;\n   189→    let comammox_alk_cost = comammox_rate * alk_per_mg_n;\n   190→    do_budget = (do_budget - comammox_o2_cost).max(0.0);\n   191→    alk_budget = (alk_budget - comammox_alk_cost).max(0.0);\n   192→\n   193→    // Apply AOB + comammox TAN consumption\n   194→    let total_tan_consumed = aob_rate + comammox_rate;\n   195→    state.water.ammonia_total_mg_n_total =\n   196→        (state.water.ammonia_total_mg_n_total - total_tan_consumed).max(0.0);\n   197→    // AOB produces nitrite\n   198→    state.water.nitrite_mg_n_total += aob_rate;\n   199→    // Comammox produces nitrate directly\n   200→    state.water.nitrate_mg_n_total += comammox_rate;\n   201→\n   202→    // Apply O2 costs so far (AOB + comammox) to state\n   203→    state.water.dissolved_oxygen_mg_total =\n   204→        (state.water.dissolved_oxygen_mg_total - aob_o2_cost - comammox_o2_cost).max(0.0);\n   205→\n   206→    // 4c. NOB: nitrite -> nitrate (uses remaining DO/alk budget)\n   207→    let nob_env_factor =\n   208→        combined_env * env.f_temp * env.f_ph * (do_budget / (do_budget + pp.nob_k_do_mg.max(0.01)));\n   209→    let nob_potential = monod_rate(\n   210→        safe_rate(pp.nob_vmax_mg_n_per_g_per_hour),\n   211→        state.microbe.nitrite_oxidizer_biomass_g,\n   212→        nob_env_factor,\n   213→        state.water.nitrite_mg_n_total,\n   214→        pp.nob_k_nitrite_mg.max(0.01),\n   215→    );\n   216→    let nob_rate = safe_rate(nob_potential)\n   217→        .min(state.water.nitrite_mg_n_total)\n   218→        .min(if o2_for_nob > 0.0 {\n   219→            do_budget / o2_for_nob\n   220→        } else {\n   221→            f64::MAX\n   222→        })\n   223→        .min(if alk_per_mg_n > 0.0 {\n   224→            alk_budget / alk_per_mg_n\n   225→        } else {\n   226→            f64::MAX\n   227→        });\n   228→\n   229→    let nob_o2_cost = nob_rate * o2_for_nob;\n   230→\n   231→    state.water.nitrite_mg_n_total = (state.water.nitrite_mg_n_total - nob_rate).max(0.0);\n   232→    state.water.nitrate_mg_n_total += nob_rate;\n   233→    state.water.dissolved_oxygen_mg_total =\n   234→        (state.water.dissolved_oxygen_mg_total - nob_o2_cost).max(0.0);\n   235→\n   236→    // Total N fully nitrified to nitrate (for alkalinity coupling)\n   237→    // AOB only takes TAN -> nitrite, NOB takes nitrite -> nitrate, comammox takes TAN -> nitrate\n   238→    // Full pathway N: nob_rate (came from AOB path) + comammox_rate\n   239→    let total_mg_n_nitrified = nob_rate + comammox_rate;\n   240→\n   241→    // ---- 5. Guild growth and decay ----\n   242→    // AOB growth from TAN oxidized\n   243→    let aob_growth = safe_rate(pp.aob_growth_yield) * aob_rate;\n   244→    let aob_decay =\n   245→        safe_rate(pp.aob_decay_rate_per_hour) * state.microbe.ammonia_oxidizer_biomass_g;\n   246→    state.microbe.ammonia_oxidizer_biomass_g =\n   247→        (state.microbe.ammonia_oxidizer_biomass_g + aob_growth - aob_decay).max(0.0);\n   248→\n   249→    // NOB growth from nitrite oxidized\n   250→    let nob_growth = safe_rate(pp.nob_growth_yield) * nob_rate;\n   251→    let nob_decay =\n   252→        safe_rate(pp.nob_decay_rate_per_hour) * state.microbe.nitrite_oxidizer_biomass_g;\n   253→    state.microbe.nitrite_oxidizer_biomass_g =\n   254→        (state.microbe.nitrite_oxidizer_biomass_g + nob_growth - nob_decay).max(0.0);\n   255→\n   256→    // Comammox growth from TAN fully oxidized\n   257→    let comammox_growth = safe_rate(pp.comammox_growth_yield) * comammox_rate;\n   258→    let comammox_decay =\n   259→        safe_rate(pp.comammox_decay_rate_per_hour) * state.microbe.comammox_biomass_g;\n   260→    state.microbe.comammox_biomass_g =\n   261→        (state.microbe.comammox_biomass_g + comammox_growth - comammox_decay).max(0.0);\n   262→\n   263→    // ---- 6. Alkalinity consumption from nitrification ----\n   264→    // AOB and comammox alkalinity was already tracked in the budget; apply the\n   265→    // total consumption (AOB + comammox + NOB path) to state.\n   266→    let total_alk_consumed = (aob_rate + comammox_rate + nob_rate) * alk_per_mg_n;\n   267→    state.water.alkalinity_meq_total =\n   268→        (state.water.alkalinity_meq_total - total_alk_consumed).max(0.0);\n   269→\n   270→    // Nitrification is a chemoautotrophic process that produces some DIC fixation\n   271→    // but for simplicity we model it as a net DIC producer via mineralization pathway above.\n   272→\n   273→    NitrogenCycleOutput {\n   274→        total_mg_n_nitrified,\n   275→    }\n   276→}\n   277→\n   278→/// Temperature factor: peaks around 25-30°C, drops off at extremes.\n   279→fn temperature_factor(temp_c: f64) -> f64 {\n   280→    // Bell-shaped factor peaking at 28°C with a half-width of ~10°C\n   281→    let opt = 28.0;\n   282→    let sigma = 10.0;\n   283→    let diff = temp_c - opt;\n   284→    (-(diff * diff) / (2.0 * sigma * sigma)).exp()\n   285→}\n   286→\n   287→/// pH factor: nitrifiers prefer 7-8, reduced at extremes.\n   288→fn ph_factor(ph: f64) -> f64 {\n   289→    let opt = 7.5;\n   290→    let sigma = 1.5;\n   291→    let diff = ph - opt;\n   292→    (-(diff * diff) / (2.0 * sigma * sigma)).exp()\n   293→}\n   294→\n   295→fn compute_env_factors(state: &TankState) -> EnvFactors {\n   296→    let f_temp = temperature_factor(state.water.temperature_c);\n   297→    let f_ph = ph_factor(state.water.ph);\n   298→\n   299→    // Maturity factor: immature filters slow nitrification\n   300→    let maturity_factor = state.filter_state.biofilter_maturity_index.clamp(0.05, 1.0);\n   301→\n   302→    // Dirty-filter factor: clogged filters reduce nitrification efficiency.\n   303→    // clogging_index of 0 = clean (factor=1), clogging_index of 1 = fully clogged (factor=0.2)\n   304→    let dirty_filter_factor = (1.0 - 0.8 * state.filter_state.clogging_index).clamp(0.2, 1.0);\n   305→\n   306→    EnvFactors {\n   307→        f_temp,\n   308→        f_ph,\n   309→        maturity_factor,\n   310→        dirty_filter_factor,\n   311→    }\n   312→}\n   313→\n   314→/// Monod-style rate: vmax * biomass * environmental_factor * S/(K+S)\n   315→fn monod_rate(\n   316→    vmax: f64,\n   317→    biomass_g: f64,\n   318→    environmental_factor: f64,\n   319→    substrate: f64,\n   320→    k_substrate: f64,\n   321→) -> f64 {\n   322→    let monod = substrate / (substrate + k_substrate);\n   323→    safe_rate(vmax * biomass_g * environmental_factor * monod)\n   324→}\n   325→\n   326→/// Daily biofilter maturity update. Called every 24 ticks.\n   327→/// Recomputes `filter_state.biofilter_maturity_index` from guild biomass.\n   328→pub fn update_daily_biofilter_maturity(state: &mut TankState) -> f64 {\n   329→    let prev = state.filter_state.biofilter_maturity_index;\n   330→\n   331→    // Capacity reference: a \"mature\" biofilter might have ~0.5g total nitrifier biomass\n   332→    let capacity_g = 0.5;\n   333→    let total_nitrifier_g = state.microbe.ammonia_oxidizer_biomass_g\n   334→        + state.microbe.nitrite_oxidizer_biomass_g\n   335→        + state.microbe.comammox_biomass_g;\n   336→    let raw_maturity = (total_nitrifier_g / capacity_g).clamp(0.0, 1.0);\n   337→\n   338→    // Smooth towards raw_maturity\n   339→    let alpha = 0.1;\n   340→    let new_maturity = (prev + alpha * (raw_maturity - prev)).clamp(0.0, 1.0);\n   341→    state.filter_state.biofilter_maturity_index = new_maturity;\n   342→\n   343→    new_maturity - prev\n   344→}\n   345→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Jkw4Aap4RXVCcRg7bgX1wz","session_id":"7c0cd9fe-375d-4881-87c2-86b174651532","uuid":"db4f1bc3-8acb-4d9b-bedf-893ce19cfbc1"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01GbPrsDhNWHC2G11EgCj2kJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01UBybsGxRq9Ht972YfipHE4","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/systems/dissolved_oxygen.rs"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":5,"cache_creation_input_tokens":431,"cache_read_input_tokens":14062,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":431,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Jkw4Aap4RXVCcRg7bgX1wz","session_id":"7c0cd9fe-375d-4881-87c2-86b174651532","uuid":"ef65dfd7-48ea-4c57-a356-8daddce5582d"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01UBybsGxRq9Ht972YfipHE4","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→use crate::{\n     2→    systems::{\n     3→        chemistry::{photosynthetic_biomass_g, respiring_biomass_g},\n     4→        temperature::do_sat_mg_l,\n     5→    },\n     6→    types::TankState,\n     7→};\n     8→\n     9→pub fn step_dissolved_oxygen(state: &mut TankState, light_on: bool) {\n    10→    let volume_l = state.geometry.water_volume_l();\n    11→    if volume_l <= f64::EPSILON {\n    12→        return;\n    13→    }\n    14→\n    15→    let do_sat_mg_l = do_sat_mg_l(state.water.temperature_c);\n    16→    let do_mg_l = state.water.dissolved_oxygen_mg_total / volume_l;\n    17→    let aeration_intensity = if state.hardware.aeration.enabled {\n    18→        state.hardware.aeration.intensity\n    19→    } else {\n    20→        0.0\n    21→    };\n    22→    let k_la = (state.process_params.reaeration_kla_base * state.geometry.top_exchange_factor())\n    23→        + (state.process_params.aeration_kla_boost * aeration_intensity);\n    24→    let delta_do_reaeration_mg = k_la * (do_sat_mg_l - do_mg_l) * volume_l;\n    25→\n    26→    let background_bod_mg = state\n    27→        .process_params\n    28→        .background_bod_mg_o2_per_g_biomass_per_hour\n    29→        * respiring_biomass_g(state);\n    30→    let photosynthetic_o2_mg = if light_on {\n    31→        state\n    32→            .process_params\n    33→            .plant_photosynthesis_o2_mg_per_g_per_hour\n    34→            * photosynthetic_biomass_g(state)\n    35→            * state.hardware.light.intensity_index\n    36→    } else {\n    37→        0.0\n    38→    };\n    39→\n    40→    state.water.dissolved_oxygen_mg_total +=\n    41→        delta_do_reaeration_mg + photosynthetic_o2_mg - background_bod_mg;\n    42→}\n    43→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Jkw4Aap4RXVCcRg7bgX1wz","session_id":"7c0cd9fe-375d-4881-87c2-86b174651532","uuid":"212b10ce-0698-48a2-8139-23324373714e"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-haiku-4-5-20251001","id":"msg_01GbPrsDhNWHC2G11EgCj2kJ","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_01Q28EDjPCg4AVj3s7aSngYQ","name":"Read","input":{"file_path":"/root/tank-simulation/crates/tank_core/src/systems/chemistry.rs"},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":5,"cache_creation_input_tokens":431,"cache_read_input_tokens":14062,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":431,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":0},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Jkw4Aap4RXVCcRg7bgX1wz","session_id":"7c0cd9fe-375d-4881-87c2-86b174651532","uuid":"fbc6e683-ee73-4221-b64f-2ffa9632afcc"}
{"type":"user","message":{"role":"user","content":[{"tool_use_id":"toolu_01Q28EDjPCg4AVj3s7aSngYQ","type":"tool_result","content":"     1→use crate::types::TankState;\n     2→\n     3→const ADULT_SHRIMP_BIOMASS_G: f64 = 0.12;\n     4→const JUVENILE_SHRIMP_BIOMASS_G: f64 = 0.05;\n     5→const ALKALINITY_FEEDBACK_MEQ_PER_MG_C: f64 = 0.0002;\n     6→\n     7→pub fn compute_ph_from_totals(\n     8→    alkalinity_meq_total: f64,\n     9→    dissolved_inorganic_carbon_mg_c_total: f64,\n    10→    volume_l: f64,\n    11→) -> f64 {\n    12→    if volume_l <= f64::EPSILON {\n    13→        return 7.0;\n    14→    }\n    15→\n    16→    let alkalinity_meq_l = alkalinity_meq_total / volume_l;\n    17→    let dic_mmol_l = (dissolved_inorganic_carbon_mg_c_total / 12.0) / volume_l;\n    18→\n    19→    (6.3 + safe_log10(alkalinity_meq_l.max(0.05)) - safe_log10(dic_mmol_l.max(0.02)))\n    20→        .clamp(5.5, 8.5)\n    21→}\n    22→\n    23→pub fn compute_nh3_mg_l(tan_mg_l: f64, ph: f64, temp_c: f64) -> f64 {\n    24→    let pka = 0.09018 + 2729.92 / (273.2 + temp_c);\n    25→    let fraction_nh3 = 1.0 / (1.0 + 10.0_f64.powf(pka - ph));\n    26→    tan_mg_l * fraction_nh3\n    27→}\n    28→\n    29→pub fn step_hourly_chemistry(state: &mut TankState, light_on: bool) {\n    30→    let volume_l = state.geometry.water_volume_l();\n    31→    if volume_l <= f64::EPSILON {\n    32→        return;\n    33→    }\n    34→\n    35→    let respiration_dic_mg = state\n    36→        .process_params\n    37→        .respiration_dic_rate_mg_c_per_g_per_hour\n    38→        * respiring_biomass_g(state);\n    39→    let photosynthesis_dic_mg = if light_on {\n    40→        state\n    41→            .process_params\n    42→            .photosynthesis_dic_rate_mg_c_per_g_per_hour\n    43→            * photosynthetic_biomass_g(state)\n    44→            * state.hardware.light.intensity_index\n    45→    } else {\n    46→        0.0\n    47→    };\n    48→    let net_dic_delta_mg = respiration_dic_mg - photosynthesis_dic_mg;\n    49→\n    50→    state.water.dissolved_inorganic_carbon_mg_c_total =\n    51→        (state.water.dissolved_inorganic_carbon_mg_c_total + net_dic_delta_mg).max(0.0);\n    52→    state.water.alkalinity_meq_total = (state.water.alkalinity_meq_total\n    53→        - (net_dic_delta_mg * ALKALINITY_FEEDBACK_MEQ_PER_MG_C))\n    54→        .max(0.0);\n    55→    state.water.ph = compute_ph_from_totals(\n    56→        state.water.alkalinity_meq_total,\n    57→        state.water.dissolved_inorganic_carbon_mg_c_total,\n    58→        volume_l,\n    59→    );\n    60→}\n    61→\n    62→pub(crate) fn respiring_biomass_g(state: &TankState) -> f64 {\n    63→    let plant_biomass_g: f64 = state.plant_guilds.iter().map(|plant| plant.biomass_g).sum();\n    64→    let algae_biomass_g = state.algae.suspended_biomass_g + state.algae.periphyton_biomass_g;\n    65→    let microbe_biomass_g = state.microbe.decomposer_biomass_g\n    66→        + state.microbe.ammonia_oxidizer_biomass_g\n    67→        + state.microbe.nitrite_oxidizer_biomass_g\n    68→        + state.microbe.comammox_biomass_g;\n    69→    let shrimp_biomass_g = (f64::from(state.animal.adults_count) * ADULT_SHRIMP_BIOMASS_G)\n    70→        + (f64::from(state.animal.juveniles_count) * JUVENILE_SHRIMP_BIOMASS_G);\n    71→\n    72→    plant_biomass_g + algae_biomass_g + microbe_biomass_g + shrimp_biomass_g\n    73→}\n    74→\n    75→pub(crate) fn photosynthetic_biomass_g(state: &TankState) -> f64 {\n    76→    let plant_biomass_g: f64 = state.plant_guilds.iter().map(|plant| plant.biomass_g).sum();\n    77→    plant_biomass_g + state.algae.periphyton_biomass_g + state.algae.suspended_biomass_g\n    78→}\n    79→\n    80→fn safe_log10(value: f64) -> f64 {\n    81→    value.max(f64::MIN_POSITIVE).log10()\n    82→}\n    83→"}]},"parent_tool_use_id":"toolu_01Jkw4Aap4RXVCcRg7bgX1wz","session_id":"7c0cd9fe-375d-4881-87c2-86b174651532","uuid":"e0b2e9eb-bdc2-4413-a538-ba3eced65b52"}
{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-4-6","id":"msg_01GDB4poHnAn85sZ7KSvSz31","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"tool_use","id":"toolu_016hwCVpQd88K2VLKsVuu4Po","name":"Agent","input":{"description":"Verify biology and events","subagent_type":"Explore","prompt":"Thoroughly verify the biology systems and events in /root/tank-simulation against these requirements:\n\n1. Plants (read crates/tank_core/src/systems/plant_growth.rs and types/biology.rs):\n   - Two guilds: FastStem and RootFeedingRosette\n   - Growth depends on: light, temperature, nitrogen, phosphorus, carbon/DIC, habitat_factor, crowding/self-shading\n   - FastStem takes nutrients from water column\n   - RootFeedingRosette draws from substrate stores\n   - Active substrate + adequate depth improves RootFeedingRosette vs inert sand\n   - Declining biomass enters detritus\n\n2. Algae/Periphyton (read systems/algae_growth.rs):\n   - Suspended algae and periphyton tracked separately\n   - Growth depends on: light, temperature, dissolved nutrients, plant competition\n   - Periphyton: provides shrimp food, nuisance risk, scales with surfaces/light, event generation when high\n\n3. Microbes/Microfauna (read systems/microfauna.rs):\n   - Decomposer biomass/capacity\n   - Nitrifier guild biomasses\n   - Aggregate microfauna grazing index\n   - Microfauna effects: increase mineralization, consume periphyton/bacterial resource, reduced by shrimp grazing\n\n4. Shrimp (read systems/shrimp.rs and types/biology.rs):\n   - Aggregate state: adults, juveniles, berried_females, condition 0..1, molt_stress 0..1, reproductive_readiness 0..1, egg_progress_days\n   - Daily condition depends on: food/periphyton, DO, NH3, nitrite, temperature, GH mineral proxy, instability\n   - Reproduction: eligible = 0.5*adults - berried, p_spawn formula, stochastic, egg development, hatch success\n   - Temperature: best 22-26C, worse by 30C, near-zero by 33C\n   - Molt stress from: low GH, abrupt changes, poor condition, thermal stress\n   - Mortality: probabilistic, increases with NH3, nitrite, low DO, heat stress, molt stress, starvation\n\n5. Substrate (read types/substrate.rs):\n   - 1-3 layers\n   - Kinds: inert_sand, inert_gravel, active_planted, coarse_porous\n   - Affects: rooted nutrient access, detritus trapping, colonizable area, low-oxygen tendency, shrimp grazing surface\n   - Substrate nutrient store for rooted plants\n   - Active substrate: higher nutrients and CEC\n\n6. Events (read types/events.rs and systems/events.rs):\n   - SimEvent struct with day, hour, severity, kind, cause_codes, summary\n   - ALL required EventKind values present\n   - Last 200 events in state, last 20 in snapshot\n\n7. Update order (read engine.rs):\n   - Hourly pipeline: 14 steps in correct order\n   - Daily pipeline: 7 steps after every 24 hourly ticks\n\nRead the actual source code and verify everything."},"caller":{"type":"direct"}}],"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":1,"cache_creation_input_tokens":2132,"cache_read_input_tokens":23943,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":2132},"output_tokens":1,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"not_available"},"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"7c0cd9fe-375d-4881-87c2-86b174651532","uuid":"7479261d-f589-47f8-b244-034b0a630434"}
